Subject: Summary: EKS Migration Discussion – Redis & PostgreSQL Decisions

Hi [Name/Team],

Here’s a summary of today’s discussion on finalizing the migration approach for AWS EKS workloads to the Azure ecosystem.

1. Redis Migration (Non-Core Workloads)

Decision:

We will proceed with two Redis instances for non-core workloads during migration:

Redis 6: For existing services such as Pricing, Notification, etc.

Redis 7: For Insights and Watchlist services.

Migration will start with Dev and UAT, followed by Production.

After migration, we will plan a separate exercise to refactor non-core services to Redis 7 for single Redis consolidation and cost optimization.

Options Evaluated:
a) Fix Insights/Watchlist to Redis 6 – saves cost but needs full QA cycle.
b) Maintain Redis 6 & 7 (as-is lift & shift) – avoids QA delay. ✅ (Chosen)
c) Upgrade all to Redis 7 – single Redis, but increases migration complexity.

Estimated Cost (Azure UK South):

Tier	Size	Approx. Monthly Cost (USD)
Standard C1 (2.5 GB)	Dev / UAT	$65–$70
Standard C2 (6 GB)	Prod	$130–$140
